          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Trademark assignment is the legal transfer of ownership of a trademark from assignor to assignee. Under the Trade Marks Act 1999, both registered and unregistered trademarks can be assigned, with or without the goodwill of the business. Must be recorded with the Trademark Registry via Form TM-P to be effective against third parties."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How to transfer trademark ownership in Pune?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Execute an assignment deed on Maharashtra stamp paper, file Form TM-P on IP India portal with the deed and documents, pay Rs 9,000 per mark (e-filing), await Registry recording by Trademark Registry Mumbai (2-6 months). Patron handles complete process including due diligence, deed drafting, and filing."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the difference between assignment and licensing?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Assignment permanently transfers ownership - assignor ceases to be proprietor. Licensing grants permission to use while licensor retains ownership. Assignment for M&A, restructuring, brand sales. Licensing for franchise, distribution, co-branding. Both require Registry recording."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can an unregistered trademark be assigned?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Under Section 39 of the Trade Marks Act 1999, unregistered trademarks can be assigned with or without goodwill. However, registering the trademark first provides the assignee with stronger enforceable rights. Patron recommends registration before assignment."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What documents are needed for trademark assignment?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Executed assignment deed (on stamp paper), trademark registration certificate or application acknowledgment, identity proofs, board resolutions from both companies, Power of Attorney, proof of consideration, Form TM-P. For assignments without goodwill: advertisement proof under Section 42."
          }
        },
        {
