</section>

<!-- SECTION 3: WHAT IS GSTAT APPEAL FILING -->
<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Is Trademark Assignment?</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>Trademark assignment is the legal transfer of ownership from assignor to assignee. Under Section 37, the registered proprietor has power to assign. Section 38 establishes that registered trademarks are assignable with or without goodwill, for all or some goods/services. Section 39 extends this to unregistered trademarks.</p><p>Key distinction: assignment with goodwill (brand + reputation transferred) vs without goodwill (mark only - subject to Section 42 conditions including mandatory advertisement). Section 40 restricts assignments creating exclusive rights in multiple persons for same/similar marks.</p><p>All assignments must be recorded via Form TM-P with Trademark Registry. Related: <a href="/trademark-registration">Trademark Registration</a>.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Trademark Assignment in Pune:</strong></p>
                    <ul><li><strong>Section 38 (Registered TM):</strong> Assignable with/without goodwill, for all or some goods/services</li><li><strong>Section 39 (Unregistered TM):</strong> Also assignable with/without goodwill. Registration recommended first</li><li><strong>Section 42 (Without Goodwill):</strong> Mandatory advertisement and Registrar approval to prevent public confusion</li><li><strong>Section 40 (Restriction):</strong> No conflicting exclusive rights in multiple persons for same marks/goods</li><li><strong>Form TM-P:</strong> Application to record assignment. Rs 9,000/mark (e-filing). Filed on ipindia.gov.in</li></ul>

                </div>
            </div>
