<!-- SECTION 8: DOCUMENTS REQUIRED -->
<section class="content-section" id="documents-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">Documents Required for Trademark Assignment</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                
                <ul><li><strong>Assignment Deed:</strong> Executed on Maharashtra stamp paper with proper consideration and goodwill specification</li><li><strong>TM Registration Certificate:</strong> Or application acknowledgment for marks being assigned</li><li><strong>Identity Proofs:</strong> PAN, Aadhaar (individuals); incorporation certificate (companies)</li><li><strong>Board Resolutions:</strong> From both assignor and assignee companies authorising the assignment</li><li><strong>Power of Attorney:</strong> In favour of trademark agent filing Form TM-P</li><li><strong>Proof of Consideration:</strong> Sale agreement, M&A agreement, or valuation report (intra-group)</li><li><strong>Form TM-P:</strong> Generated on IP India e-filing portal</li><li><strong>NOC from Licensees:</strong> If trademark has registered users or licensees</li><li><strong>Advertisement Proof:</strong> For assignments without goodwill (Section 42)</li></ul><p style="margin-top:16px;"><strong>Pune startup tip:</strong> When transferring founder's trademark to company, clearly state consideration (even nominal Rs 1) and include goodwill. Document properly to avoid disputes during M&A or exit.</p>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

