<!-- SECTION 15A: LEGAL FRAMEWORK -->
<section class="content-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">Legal Framework for Trademark Assignment</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                
                <p><strong>Sections 37-45 Trade Marks Act 1999:</strong> Assignment and transmission provisions. S.37: power to assign. S.38: registered TM assignable with/without goodwill. S.39: unregistered TM assignable. S.40: restriction on conflicting rights. S.42: conditions for without goodwill. S.45: Registry recording. Source: <a href="https://ipindia.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ipindia.gov.in</a></p><p><strong>Rules 68-74 Trade Marks Rules 2017:</strong> Procedure for Form TM-P. Fee Rs 9,000 (e-filing) or Rs 10,000 (paper). Jurisdictional office: TM Registry Mumbai for Maharashtra.</p><p><strong>Stamp Duty and Tax:</strong> Maharashtra stamp duty on deed. Capital gains on IP transfer (S.48-55 Income Tax Act). GST on assignment consideration if applicable. Source: <a href="https://www.wipo.int/wipolex/en/text/128107" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WIPO</a></p>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

