            <div class="faq-expanded">
                <aside class="faq-expanded__aside">
                    <h2 class="faq-expanded__title">Frequently Asked Questions - Trademark Assignment in Pune</h2>
                    <p class="faq-expanded__lead">Answers about trademark transfer, assignment types, with/without goodwill, documents, costs, timeline, and assignment vs licensing for Pune businesses.</p>
                    @include('partials.bigin-form', [
                        'variant'  => 'compact',
                        'service'  => 'Trademark Assignment in Pune',
                        'city'     => 'Pune',
                    ])
                </aside>
                <div class="faq-expanded__list">
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is trademark assignment?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Trademark assignment is the legal transfer of ownership of a trademark from assignor to assignee. Under the Trade Marks Act 1999, both registered and unregistered trademarks can be assigned, with or without the goodwill of the business. Must be recorded with the Trademark Registry via Form TM-P to be effective against third parties.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How to transfer trademark ownership in Pune?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Execute an assignment deed on Maharashtra stamp paper, file Form TM-P on IP India portal with the deed and documents, pay Rs 9,000 per mark (e-filing), await Registry recording by Trademark Registry Mumbai (2-6 months). Patron handles complete process including due diligence, deed drafting, and filing.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is the difference between assignment and licensing?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Assignment permanently transfers ownership - assignor ceases to be proprietor. Licensing grants permission to use while licensor retains ownership. Assignment for M&A, restructuring, brand sales. Licensing for franchise, distribution, co-branding. Both require Registry recording.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can an unregistered trademark be assigned?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. Under Section 39 of the Trade Marks Act 1999, unregistered trademarks can be assigned with or without goodwill. However, registering the trademark first provides the assignee with stronger enforceable rights. Patron recommends registration before assignment.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What documents are needed for trademark assignment?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Executed assignment deed (on stamp paper), trademark registration certificate or application acknowledgment, identity proofs, board resolutions from both companies, Power of Attorney, proof of consideration, Form TM-P. For assignments without goodwill: advertisement proof under Section 42.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How much does trademark assignment cost?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Government fee: Rs 9,000 per mark (e-filing). Professional fees: Rs 14,999-24,999 per mark (complete package). M&A portfolio: Rs 24,999-49,999. Founder-to-company: Rs 9,999-14,999. Maharashtra stamp duty additional, based on consideration value.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-7">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is assignment with and without goodwill?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>With goodwill: trademark transfers along with business reputation and customer associations. Without goodwill: mark transfers but business/reputation stays with assignor - subject to Section 42 conditions (mandatory advertisement, Registrar approval to prevent confusion). Most M&A involves with goodwill.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-8">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How long does trademark assignment take?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Deed execution: 3-7 days (including due diligence). Form TM-P filing: 1-2 days. Registry recording: 2-6 months (Trademark Registry Mumbai processing). Post-recording updates: 1-2 weeks. Total: 3-7 months. Deed is effective between parties immediately upon execution.</p></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>


            <!-- Quick Answers -->
            <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:32px;">
                <p><strong>Quick Answers</strong></p>
                <p><strong>Trademark kaise transfer hota hai Pune mein?</strong> Assignment deed banao (Maharashtra stamp paper pe), Form TM-P IP India portal pe file karo, Rs 9,000/mark fee. TM Registry Mumbai record karegi 2-6 mahine mein. Patron Pune se handle karta hai.</p><p><strong>Founder ka TM company mein kaise transfer karein?</strong> Assignment deed (founder = assignor, company = assignee), consideration mention karo (Rs 1 bhi chalega), goodwill include karo, Form TM-P file karo. Funding round se pehle zaroori hai.</p><p><strong>Assignment aur licensing mein kya fark hai?</strong> Assignment = permanent ownership transfer. Licensing = temporary use permission (owner wahi rehta hai). M&A mein assignment. Franchise mein licensing.</p>

